# Licensing

This repository holds four different kinds of material and they are not under the same
terms. Read the category before you reuse anything.

## 1. Original writing — CC BY 4.0

Every article, explainer, README, and note written for this project. This includes
`web/content/`, `reference/`, `the_players/`, `files/*.md`, and the directory READMEs
throughout the archive.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, full text in
`LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0`. Use it, quote it, republish it, build on it — commercially or not —
with credit to abigcloud.com.

SPDX identifier: `CC-BY-4.0`.

## 2. Original code — MIT

Every script and site component written for this project: `files/bin/`, `web/src/`,
`web/scripts/`, and the Astro configuration.

Licensed under the MIT License, full text in `LICENSE-MIT`.

SPDX identifier: `MIT`.

## 3. Government records — no rights claimed

State audits, Comptroller PILOT and debt reports, IRS Form 990 filings, council agendas and
minutes, property assessments, Secretary of State filings, statutes, and every other public
record in this archive.

These are public records. **No copyright is claimed over them and none could be.** They are
reproduced here exactly as filed, because a citation to a document nobody can open is not a
citation. Anyone may use them freely. Their being here confers no rights on this project and
implies no endorsement by the agencies that produced them.

The text extractions under `derived/` are machine output from those same public records and
are treated identically.

## 4. Third-party copyrighted material — rights reserved by their owners

News articles, trade publications, press releases, podcast transcripts, scanned newspaper
pages, and saved web pages produced by other people and organizations. Found in
`web_articles/`, `podcasts/transcripts/`, and among the saved pages in the archive.

**These are not licensed by this project and are not ours to license.** They are retained as
archival copies for reference, verification, and comparison against later versions — the
ordinary practice of documenting what a source said and when. Copyright remains with the
publishers and authors named in each file's provenance header.

If you own one of these and want it removed, open an issue on
`github.com/kissmyfix/abigcloud` and it will be taken down.

---

*Written 2026-08-19. A single CC BY 4.0 file previously sat at the repository root, which
had the effect of purporting to license public records and other publishers' work under
terms this project has no standing to grant. That file is now `LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0` and covers
category 1 only.*
